# Trivy ignore list — CVEs we cannot action yet, so they don't hard-fail CI.
#
# These live in the `syft` binary bundled into the runtime image. syft vendors
# go-git / go-billy versions affected by the CVEs below. Fixes exist upstream
# (go-git >= 5.19.0 / 5.19.1, go-billy >= 5.9.0), but the latest syft release
# (v1.44.0) has not yet bumped them — so there is no syft version we can build
# that resolves these today. Real-world risk is low: we run syft only against
# our own build context to generate an SBOM, not against untrusted remote
# repositories or crafted symlink trees.
#
# Renovate tracks SYFT_VERSION (Dockerfile + ci.yml). When syft ships a release
# with the patched dependencies, bump SYFT_VERSION and delete the matching
# entries below — the image scan will then enforce them again.

# go-git: improper single-quote escaping in SSH transport
CVE-2026-45570
# go-git: crafted repositories may modify main and submodule .git directories
CVE-2026-45571
# go-git: improper parsing of crafted objects (inconsistent vs upstream Git)
CVE-2026-45022
# go-billy: missing depth/cycle detection in symlink resolution (resource exhaustion)
CVE-2026-44740
# go-billy: path traversal vulnerabilities
CVE-2026-44973
